SUMMARY:Saturday Freethought Conversations
DESCRIPTION:Lancaster Freethought Society\n**July 25 Discussion: Living Ou
 r Values -**\n***How Do We Put Freedom\, Reason & Inquiry Into Action?***\
 n\nValues are not just words we agree with.\nThey become real through habi
 ts\, choices\, communities\, and action.\nFor this final discussion in our
  four-part series\, we’ll use the LFS member survey as our guide. Member
 s told us they want more small discussion groups\, day trips and cultural 
 outings\, speaker events\, book discussions\, freethought conversations\, 
 and community connection.\n\nSo we’ll ask:\n**What should LFS try next?*
 *\n**How do good ideas become real events?**\n**How can we turn freethough
 t values into action?**\n\nWe’ll also talk about the survey’s stronges
 t topic result: **aging\, friendship\, and community**. What does secular 
 community look like when people need belonging\, meaning\, friendship\, an
 d support without religion?\n\n**Discussion format:**\nTimed rounds\, up t
 o 2 minutes each\, option to pass\, no interruptions\, with open discussio
 n after every 2 rounds.\n**Come curious. Come ready to listen.**\n\n**Even
 t Participation Standard**\n\nThis event welcomes open inquiry and diverse
  viewpoints within a foundation of equality\, human dignity\, and democrac
 y. Racist\, sexist\, fascist\, anti-LGBTQ\, or other ideologies that deny 
 anyone’s equal rights are not welcome or open for debate. Participants w
 ill not be required to defend or debate their humanity or equality. The or
 ganizer may interrupt or remove anyone whose words or conduct violate thes
 e boundaries.
