SUMMARY:Patriarchy\, Matriarchy & Democracy: A Two-Part Online Discussion
DESCRIPTION:Lancaster Freethought Society\n**A Two-Part Online Discussion:
  Can Democracy Survive a Patriarchy?**\nThis is an LFS online discussion s
 eries\, held on Google Meet.\n\nAcross two sessions\, we’ll explore how 
 patriarchy and matriarchy organize power\, care\, law\, family\, sex\, mon
 ey\, violence\, and democracy.\nWe’ll use consciousness-raising style di
 scussion rules: speak personally\, listen carefully\, don’t interrupt\, 
 and don’t debate someone while they are speaking.\n\nFor each question\,
  we’ll do a speaking round first. After everyone who wants to speak has 
 spoken\, Susan will offer brief evidence\, examples\, or definitions to de
 epen the discussion.\n\n**Part 1**\n\n* What is patriarchy?\n* What is mat
 riarchy?\n* How do these systems operate?\n\n**Part 2**\n\n* What are the 
 benefits of each?\n* What are the dangers or pitfalls of each?\n* Can demo
 cracy survive a patriarchy — or does real democracy require a different 
 social order?\n\nThis is not a lecture. It is a structured conversation.\n
 \n**Google Meet link:** The Google Meet link will be sent on the day and o
 nly to members who RSVP “Yes.” Please RSVP if you plan to attend.\n\nT
 his event welcomes open inquiry and diverse viewpoints within a foundation
  of equality\, human dignity\, and democracy. Racist\, sexist\, fascist\, 
 anti-LGBTQ\, or other ideologies that deny anyone’s equal rights are not
  welcome or open for debate. Participants will not be required to defend o
 r debate their humanity or equality. The organizer may interrupt or remove
  anyone whose words or conduct violate these boundaries.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/lancaster-freethought-society/events/
 315514104/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260702T124103Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260702T124103Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
